elected leaders in Washington State may  crack down on vaccine exemptions amid a  growing measles outbreak lawmakers are  proposing a bill that would no longer  allow parents to cite philosophical or  personal reasons for not vaccinating  their child currently 18 states allow  those exemptions and Carter Evans is at  the State Capitol in Olympia where a  public hearing will take place today  Carter good morning good morning the  governor has declared a state of  emergency here as the number of measles  infections continues to rise there are  now 56 cases here in the Pacific  Northwest and lawmakers are hoping to  pass a bill that will insure more  children are vaccinated right now my  city is the hotbed for this outbreak  monica Stonier is the state  representative for Clark County  Washington the area hardest hit by the  measles outbreak in her County alone  there are currently 51 confirmed cases  of measles and another 13 suspected it  certainly has reached a critical stage  in my County Stonier is now  co-sponsoring a bipartisan House bill  that would require every child at every  public and private school in the state  and licensed daycare center to be  vaccinated for measles mumps and rubella  unless they have a legitimate medical or  religious exemption if you would have  asked me four years ago I would have  told you that yeah every child needs  their axons Abigail Lockhart refuses to  vaccinate her youngest child she says  it's because her middle child suffered  significant behavioral and physical  reactions after being vaccinated  including severe eczema and food  allergies if I could go back I wouldn't  have vaccinated any of my kids  according to the CDC most people who get  the vaccine do not have any serious  health problems the agency also says for  every 1000 children who get the measles  one or two will die from it the benefits  of the vaccine greatly outweigh the  risks dan Salman is the former director  of vaccine safety for Health and Human  Services  he said measles can cause lifelong  complications no one knows that better  than Cecilia Rodriguez in 1989 she was  too young to be vaccinated when she  contracted the German measles I can end  it for me it became a lifetime  Rodriguez spent nine months in a coma  and almost died thirty years later her  eyesight speech and hearing are still  affected I do not want to go through  that experience with my three three  beautiful children that I have Salman  says in a way vaccines are a victim of  their own success because most people  have never seen the measles people  aren't afraid of what they don't know  and we'd like to keep it that way  people on both sides of the issue are  expected to speak at what could be a  very fiery hearing today lawmakers are  hoping to determine if they have enough  votes to move forward gale we shall see  Thank You Carter
 

